# This directory holds per-run lockfiles (one per run_id).
# The lockfile history is part of the audit trail per the
# README's "Commit discipline" section; the directory itself
# is reserved by the .gitkeep placeholder so the structure
# is preserved in the initial commit and so `git clone` always
# creates the directory.
#
# Per-run lockfiles are created at run start and either removed
# at clean run end or kept for forensics on FAILED runs. The
# runs/.gitignore does NOT ignore *.lock by default because
# the lock-acquisition history is forensic data.
